 line through $r = 0$ on which the isotropic radius is $r = |x|$. The metric on it is $-e^{-2m/|x|}c^2dt^2 + e^{2m/|x|}dx^2$, the same on both halves, and no Christoffel symbol turns the rays out of the plane, so they are null geodesics.","The halves $x > 0$ and $x < 0$ lie in one asymptotically flat region, on opposite sides of the wormhole's mouth, and each has the throat at $|x| = m$. A ray moving toward $x = 0$ crosses the throat and the cones then close on it as $e^{-2m/|x|}$, so no ray drawn passes from one half to the other. The far end of the wormhole, $r = 0$, is the single point $x = 0$ of this line, and the spheres around it grow without bound as they near it."],"source":{"fields":["coords","parameters","metric_components","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","domains"],"version":"67aaeae487b42d95"},"slices":[{"view":"wormhole","surface":0,"label":"$t = 0$","version":"b495348cfb50d868","lines":[[[0.0,0.5],[0.4583,0.5]],[[0.5417,0.5],[1.0,0.5]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[1.0,0.5],"anchor":"br","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}}]}],"areal":[{"id":"radial","label":"$t$ and $R$","plane":["t","R"],"families":["ingoing","outgoing"],"xlabel":"$R/m$","ylabel":"$ct/m$","ticks":{"x":[{"at":3.0,"label":"$3$"},{"at":4.0,"label":"$4$"},{"at":5.0,"label":"$5$"},{"at":6.0,"label":"$6$"}],"y":[{"at":-2.0,"label":"$-2$"},{"at":-1.0,"label":"$-1$"},{"at":0.0,"label":"$0$"},{"at":1.0,"label":"$1$"},{"at":2.0,"label":"$2$"}]},"box":[2.718281828459045,6.718281828459045,-2,2],"to_display":[[0.0,1.0],[1.0,0.0]],"mirror":false,"rays":{"P":[[[0.0364,-0.0213],[0.0279,0.0432],[0.0203,0.1102],[0.0141,0.1774],[0.009,0.2447],[0.005,0.3146],[0.0023,0.3846],[0.0,0.5295]],[[0.1055,-0.0208],[0.08,0.0862],[0.0587,0.1915],[0.0405,0.3],[0.0259,0.409],[0.0145,0.521],[0.0065,0.6357],[0.0016,0.7556],[0.0,0.8781]],[[0.1737,-0.0204],[0.153,0.0439],[0.1342,0.1061],[0.1166,0.1687],[0.1003,0.2316],[0.0852,0.2948],[0.0719,0.3559],[0.0594,0.4197],[0.0481,0.4837],[0.0381,0.5479],[0.0293,0.6123],[0.021